The top of each page you reached with Ctrl-PgDn and Ctrl-PgUp was displayed
in the middle of your screen.  This lets you see the end of one page and the
first part of the next page.

Instead of having to find a title to get back to this page, it is more
convenient for you to keep track of your place by checking the "status line"
at the very bottom of the screen.  The page number is next to the letter "P"
on the far right.  "L" and "C" show you the line and column number of the
cursor's position on that page.

The bottom of each page is marked by a line or reverse video.

