                               ENTERING TEXT

Now you try typing some text.  Don't worry if you make a mistake while
typing.  You can use the Backspace key to delete the wrong characters and
retype.  Backspace is above the Enter key, marked with an arrow  <--  .


..LAYOUT 2  
   =>  Place the cursor on the first blank line below, and start typing some
       text (for example, retype this paragraph).  As you reach the right
       margin, continue typing, and let Volkswriter take care of adjusting
       the line ending for you.
..LAYOUT 1  







What you have just seen is "word wrap."  Volkswriter watches your line
length as you type, and "wraps" the text down to the next line when you
reach the margin.  So you never need to think about line length as you type.
Instead, make it a habit to press the Enter key (also called Return) when
you reach the end of a paragraph.  This indicates that the line or lines you
have just entered should remain separate from other paragraphs.


..page

                             MAKING CORRECTIONS

One of the nicest things about a word processor is that you can begin
writing without worrying about being letter-perfect, and then you can edit
later to get it just right.  Let's see how easy it is.

Before you start the exercise below, look at the cursor:  it should be a
blinking horizontal line.  If it is a small blinking square instead, press
the key marked Ins on the lower right of your keyboard (press it once,
briefly).


           This setnence contains two mistaks....

..LAYOUT 2  
   =>  Move the cursor to "t" in "setnence" above.  Type the letters "nt" to
       correct the word.

   =>  Move the cursor to last letter of "mistaks," where you need to insert
       the letter "e".  Press the Ins key once, so the cursor becomes a
       small blinking square.  You have now turned on Insert mode.  With the
       cursor under the "s" type the letter "e" so the word reads
       "mistakes".

   =>  Move the cursor under the "m" of "mistakes," and type the word
       "spelling " (include the space after the word).

   =>  Finally, move the cursor under the first period and press the key
       marked Del three times, to delete the extra periods.


..LAYOUT 1  
These are a few of the ways of correcting text.  If you want to continue
experimenting, use the text above.

You now know two methods for deleting characters -- using the Backspace key
or the Delete key.  Both methods will continue deleting characters very
rapidly if you hold down the key.

Notice the difference between correcting with Backspace when Insert is on
and when it is off.  With Insert on, characters to the right of the cursor
move back with it when you press the Backspace key.  When Insert is off,
they do not move.  Try it!

And, by the way . . . the Volkswriter 3 spelling program would have found
both of the mistakes in the sample paragraph.  We'll try spelling correction
in another tutorial.


..page

                            GETTING THERE FASTER

There are faster ways to move to a specific place where you want to add text
or correct it.


..LAYOUT 2  
   =>  Move the cursor to this line.  Hold the Ctrl key down and press the
       Cursor-right key two or three times.  Watch as the cursor moves to
       the right, one word at a time.

..LAYOUT 3  
       Then try holding Ctrl-Cursor-right down instead of just pressing it
       and see what happens.  After the cursor reaches the last word in the
       line, it jumps down to the next line.

       Now try the same thing with the Ctrl key and the Cursor-left.  The
       cursor moves left a word at a time, jumping up a line when it reaches
       the left of the screen.


..LAYOUT 1  
For large moves in a document, the Home key is used to "amplify" the effect
of the arrow keys.


..LAYOUT 2  
   =>  Try pressing the Home key (press and release this key, don't hold it
       down).  Then press Cursor-up. The cursor moves to the top of the
       screen while remaining in the same column.

..LAYOUT 3  
       Now try the Home - Cursor-down combination (again, press and release
       the Home key, then press Cursor-down).  The cursor jumps to the
       bottom of the screen.  Home - Cursor-left moves the cursor to the
       beginning of the line; Home - Cursor-right moves it to the end.


..LAYOUT 1  
Home - Home (i.e., pressing Home twice) moves the cursor to the top line of
the screen, at the current left margin.  Pressing Home a third time (Home -
Home - Home) moves the cursor to the first line of the first page.  Home
- End takes you to the last line of the last page.


If you press Home by mistake, don't worry.  Pressing any key other than
those listed cancels the Home key.

