                         TO EXIT THE FIRST TUTORIAL


Before we leave, a word on storing files.  Until a document has been
"stored" on a disk using the S option in the Main Menu, none of the changes
or additions you have made are permanent.  In other words, all changes or
new writing exist only in the computer's memory.  You must store the changes
on disk before you turn off your computer, or they will be lost.

Volkswriter 3 reminds you of the hazard if you try to do anything that can
cause your changes to be lost.

However, DO NOT STORE THESE TUTORIALS when you are prompted, or all your
deletions and experimentations will become permanent.  The original tutorial
files should remain intact on disk so you can refer to them again or print
them.

You have finished the first tutorial.  Here's how to exit, and, if you are
ready, continue with the next tutorial:

